Kind: ablation
Issue: #712
Takes out: both halves of the rule for a list longer than its bytes, as the defect was -- the server hands the whole list over, and virtio builds a descriptor for every page given, of length 0 past the bytes, at which QEMU marks the device broken.  cap_test [14] finds virtio_blk0a failing the long list, or answering no read after it.  Either half alone is a whole guard: the other one would hide its absence.
Run: --entry 14 600 -smp 4
Expect: cap_test: \[14\] WRONG — virtio_blk0a (did not serve 4096 bytes through a list one page longer|served a list one page longer than its bytes, and then did not answer)

